## 9. Testing Examples

### 9.1 Create Organization (First Time)

**Request:**
```graphql
mutation {
  createOrUpdateBuyerOrganization(input: {
    orgName: "Acme Corp"
    orgIndustry: "Technology & Software"
    location: "San Francisco, CA"
    orgDescription: "Leading enterprise technology solutions company..."
    orgLogoImages: ["uploads/organization/logo.png"]
  }) {
    _id
    orgName
    orgIndustry
  }
}
```

**Expected:** Creates new organization, returns with `_id`

### 9.2 Update Organization (After Creation)

**Request:** Same as above, but organization already exists

**Expected:** Updates existing organization, returns updated object

### 9.3 Upload Logo

**Request:** Multipart form-data (see section 2.1)

**Expected:** Returns image URL string (e.g., `"uploads/organization/uuid-filename.jpg"`)

### 9.4 Create Service Request

**Request:**
```graphql
mutation {
  createServiceRequest(input: {
    reqBuyerOrgId: "org123"
    reqTitle: "Web Design & Brand Identity Refresh"
    reqDescription: "We need a complete redesign..."
    reqCategory: "Design & Creative"
    reqSubCategory: "Visual Identity & Branding"
    reqBudgetMin: 4500
    reqBudgetMax: 6000
    reqDeadline: "2024-12-31T00:00:00Z"
    reqUrgency: URGENT
    reqSkillsNeeded: ["Figma", "Photoshop", "Brand Guidelines"]
    reqStatus: DRAFT
  }) {
    _id
    reqTitle
    reqStatus
  }
}
```

**Expected:** Creates service request with status DRAFT

### 9.5 Get Service Requests

**Request:**
```graphql
query {
  getBuyerServiceRequests(input: {
    status: OPEN
    page: 1
    limit: 10
    sortBy: "createdAt"
    sortOrder: "desc"
  }) {
    list {
      _id
      reqTitle
      reqStatus
      reqTotalQuotes
    }
    metaCounter {
      total
      open
    }
  }
}
```

**Expected:** Returns filtered and paginated list with meta counters

